    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good high-level summary, but I need more granular detail for our screening rubrics. When we say \"commanding authority\" or \"gravitas,\" what does that actually look like in practice during a boardroom presentation? Can you break down the specific vocal qualities, body language, and even the general grooming or aesthetic standards that signal this kind of high-level executive presence? We want to ensure our assessors can spot it instantly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
