      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While there is no single \"unwritten rule\" for grooming, candidates with high-level gravitas typically prioritize impeccable, polished attire (such as a tailored suit) that conveys professionalism without being overly ostentatious. Their vocal patterns often feature a deliberate pace, a clear enunciation, and a steady tone that projects calm confidence rather than fragmented or overly aggressive speech. Crucially, their body language should anchor them through the room with open, purposeful gestures and steady eye contact, actively listening rather than just waiting to speak. These specific non-verbal cues combined with a synthesized vision of the organization are what an evaluator will look for to distinguish true executive presence from general competence.",
